#
# Shared camera state for the stock OnePlus 7 Pro camera.
#
# The stock build has no camera-specific init script: its SELinux policy labels
# /data/vendor/camera as vendor_data_file and the app carries the
# vendor_data_file exemption, so the directory only has to exist once the HAL
# creates it.
#
# This port runs the app in its own opluscamera_app domain and labels the path
# oplus_camera_data_file, so the directory has to exist with the right owner
# and security context before the first write.
#
# init's mkdir applies mode, uid and gid but not the SELinux label, so each
# directory needs an explicit restorecon. Without it the first write from
# cameraserver or the app is denied and the camera still works only because the
# path happens to inherit a label from its parent.
#
# mkdir already applies the owner and mode; the explicit chmod/chown would only
# repeat it.
#

on post-fs-data
    mkdir /data/vendor/camera 0770 system camera
    restorecon /data/vendor/camera
    mkdir /data/vendor/camera/occe 0770 system camera
    restorecon /data/vendor/camera/occe
